From 5d1b5264f75a822f238c29117ae0af3babd73a7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jelon <jelon@tbu.net>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:03:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(oxfmt): pure Rust build supports --lsp and
 --stdin-filepath

Why: the pure Rust binary already formats JS/TS/CSS/Markdown/YAML/Vue natively, but only the napi entry exposed LSP and stdin, so editors had to start Node.

Both entry points now compile without the napi feature; JS/TS config files and Prettier-only languages (mdx, svelte, astro, ...) stay unsupported there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
